.Pp
Options are read until the first argument that does not begin
with
.Ql "-" .
That argument is the
.Ar script ,
and every argument after it is passed to the script without
being read as an option.
Once the script has run,
.Nm
calls the
.Ql "main"
function it defines,
if any,
with the script’s path followed by
.Ar args .
The same list is bound to
.Ql "*args*" .
With no
.Ar script ,
and no
.Fl e ,
.Ic run
starts a REPL.
.Pp
An error that a
.Ar script ,
a module loaded with
.Fl l
or code given to
.Fl e
does not handle ends the process with status 1.
.Pp
The options are applied in a fixed order,
whatever order they are written in:
first the settings (\c
.Fl d ,
.Fl c ,
.Fl C ,
.Fl s ,
.Fl r ,
.Fl q
and
.Fl i ) ,
then
.Fl l ,
then
.Fl e ,
and last the
.Ar script .
A setting therefore applies to every library,
expression and script,
and
.Fl l
runs before every
.Fl e .
Several
.Fl e
options and several
.Fl l
options run in the order given.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl e ,
.Fl "-eval"
.Ar code
.Xc
Evaluate
.Ar code
as Wattle source.
The REPL is not started afterwards unless
.Fl r
is also given.
.It Xo
.Fl l ,
.Fl "-lib"
.Ar module
.Xc
Import
.Ar module
into the environment before continuing,
without a prefix,
so its bindings are available to later options,
the
.Ar script
and the REPL.
.It Xo
.Fl i ,
.Fl "-img"
.Xc
Treat
.Ar script
as an image made by
.Ic build img
rather than as source,
load it and call its
.Ql "main"
function.
.It Xo
.Fl r ,
.Fl "-repl"
.Xc
Start the REPL after the
.Ar script
or the other options have run.
.It Xo
.Fl s ,
.Fl "-stdin"
.Xc
Read REPL input as raw lines from standard input and write prompts
to standard output.
Implies
.Fl r .
.It Xo
.Fl d ,
.Fl "-debug"
.Xc
Set
.Ql "*debug*"
and
.Ql "*redef*" .
An error in the REPL enters the debugger,
and a top-level definition can be rebound.
.It Xo
.Fl q ,
.Fl "-quiet"
.Xc
Do not print the banner when the REPL starts.
.It Xo
.Fl c ,
.Fl "-color"
.Xc
Print values,
errors and documentation with ANSI colour,
and highlight the source typed at the REPL.
If
.Fl C
is also given,
.Fl C
applies.
.It Xo
.Fl C ,
.Fl "-no-color"
.Xc
Print values,
errors and documentation without ANSI colour,
and do not highlight the source typed at the REPL.
.El
